usage: capture_enemy_feedback_01_remains.py [-h] --output OUTPUT --variant
                                            {before,after} [--seed SEED]
                                            [--chain {underworld,legacy}]
                                            [--expect-remains]
                                            [--compare-trace COMPARE_TRACE]
                                            [--expect-disappear]

Record accepted death and a 3.5-second corpse hold in a named rendering chain.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT
  --variant {before,after}
                        Label only. Run unchanged driver against the intended
                        source externally.
  --seed SEED
  --chain {underworld,legacy}
  --expect-remains      Require a visible, settled, stationary final 3.5s per
                        case; validation only.
  --compare-trace COMPARE_TRACE
  --expect-disappear    Require an accepted death visual, then a fully
                        invisible final tail (v5 user direction).
